e:["$","p",null,{"className":"intro-explanation","children":["The interpretation layer is the mechanism proposed in ",["$","a",null,{"className":"text-link","href":"https://yspbob.github.io/AI-Playbook/AI_Engineering_Playbook.html#4-the-interpretation-layer","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":"Chapter 4 of the AI Engineering Playbook"}],". It should help agents understand the rules behind a system. Before testing whether it helps them write code, we need to see what it actually produces."]}]
f:["$","a",null,{"className":"text-link intro-jump","href":"/interpretation-layer-poc/progress/","children":["See progress and the next step ",["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M5 12h14","key":"1ays0h"}],["path",{"d":"m12 5 7 7-7 7","key":"xquz4c"}]],"className":"lucide-arrow-right","size":16}]]}]
10:["$","aside",null,{"className":"hypothesis","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"THE RESULT OF THIS PHASE"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"A guide we can inspect, with evidence for its claims and an independent assessment."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"hypothesis-explanation","children":"The report will show correct rules, missing rules, unsupported claims and unresolved questions. A fluent explanation or a list of citations will not be enough."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"hypothesis-foot","children":"Testing the guide in a coding task comes in Phase 2."}]]}]
11:["$","section",null,{"className":"section-block","id":"method","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"section-no","children":"01"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"THE WORK IN THIS PHASE"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"From project evidence to an assessed guide"}]]}]]}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"method-steps","children":[["$","li",null,{"className":"method-step","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"method-step-number","children":"1"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Choose the evidence and establish what it supports"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-content","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Select one repository and a few different kinds of decisions. For each, establish the applicable rule, exceptions and any uncertainty using project records and reproducible behaviour."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Prepare separate files for the layer and for assessment. The layer receives only its permitted project evidence. The assessment record stays hidden."}],["$","$L16",null,{"children":["$","$L17",null,{"id":"source-access","title":"What can the layer read?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Use a fixed code version and the project instructions that actually applied to it. Record every supplied file and the reason it belongs in the input. Do not select files to hint at a hidden answer."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Some cases will expose a rule in documentation; others may require interpreting code. Record that distinction for each claim. Never remove applicable project instructions to manufacture an inference test."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"If the evidence cannot establish a central requirement, leave that case out of scored assessment. Record it as unresolved."}]]}]}]]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"method-step","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"method-step-number","children":"2"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Ask the drafter to prepare guidance"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-content","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"The drafter is the part of the interpretation layer that proposes rules. It explains what each rule means, where it applies, what supports it and where an exception or uncertainty remains."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"It does not receive a later coding task or the assessment answers. We keep its original draft so that mistakes remain visible even if they are corrected later."}]]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"method-step","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"method-step-number","children":"3"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Check the draft against its evidence"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-content","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"A separate verifier checks the drafter’s claims. It can accept a supported claim, request a correction or leave it unresolved. Any permitted revisions follow limits fixed before the run."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Save both the draft and the accepted guide, together with the verifier’s decisions. Acceptance means that the verifier found evidence support. It is not approval from a project owner."}]]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"method-step","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"method-step-number","children":"4"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Assess the guidance independently"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-content","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"A separate assessment uses the hidden reference evidence to examine the draft, the accepted guide and the verifier’s decisions. The verifier cannot judge its own success."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Check what the guide got right, what it missed and what it asserted without support. Also check whether the verifier accepted a bad claim or rejected a valid one. Record preparation time, cost and failed attempts."}],"$L18"]}]]}]]}]]}]
12:["$","section",null,{"className":"phase-scope","id":"phase-deliverable","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"WHAT WE WILL HAVE"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"A result we can examine before building more."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"A versioned guide, its claim evidence, the original draft, the verifier’s decisions and an independent assessment. The report includes omissions, failures, uncertainty and preparation costs."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"The decision at the end"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Decide whether the guide is defensible enough to test in a coding task, whether preparation needs repair or whether to stop. A positive result is not required to finish this phase."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"This phase can establish the quality of the guidance in the tested cases. It cannot show that the guidance improves code or pays for itself."}]]}]]}]
13:["$","section",null,{"className":"section-block","id":"phase-controls","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"section-no","children":"02"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"KEEPING THE TEST CREDIBLE"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"Build the controls this phase actually uses"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-intro","children":"The drafter, verifier and independent assessor need separate contexts and explicit access boundaries. We must record what each received and prevent hidden assessment material from reaching the working roles."}],["$","$L16",null,{"children":[["$","$L17",null,{"id":"phase-technology","title":"What needs to be built now, and what can wait?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Now we need permitted input packs, isolated role calls, bounded outputs, records of decisions and costs, and protected assessment material. Any tool exposed to a role must pass the relevant boundary tests before use."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Start with controlled reading of supplied files. Coding agents, automated code review and the interactive checker belong to later phases. We do not need to implement them to assess a guide."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"If an agent is allowed to execute code to inspect a source, that capability needs the full execution restrictions and testing before it is enabled. Deferring coding tasks does not waive containment for tools we actually expose."}],["$","p",null,{"children":["$","a",null,{"className":"text-link","href":"/interpretation-layer-poc/trial-method/#technical-setup","children":"Read the proposed setup for the complete trial."}]}]]}],["$","$L17",null,{"id":"familiarity","title":"Could the model already know the public project?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Yes. Separate probes will look for signs of familiarity during repository and case selection. They cannot prove that the model has never seen the code. Results must distinguish evidence supplied in the run from possible prior knowledge."}],[["$","p",null,{"children":"Asking a model whether it recognises a project is not enough. The experiment will look for observable recall in two separate checks, at the relevant selection stage. Repository checks belong to Phase 1; historical fix reconstruction belongs to selecting coding tasks for Phase 2."}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"plain-list","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"When screening repositories:"}]," give the model a short excerpt with a distinctive detail removed, such as unusual comment wording or an arbitrary test value. Ask it to recover the missing detail. Include comparable, newly written snippets to see how often it can guess without prior exposure."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"When selecting historical tasks:"}]," give the model a limited task description, with no repository access, and ask where and how it would make the change. Compare the answer with distinctive details of the historical fix that were not supplied in the prompt."]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"A conventional correct solution could come from reasoning. Reproducing unusual details is more suggestive of recall. Neither test can prove that the model has never seen the material."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"We will set the questions, scoring rules and number of attempts before running these checks. We will use the exact model versions intended for the experiment."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Each check runs in a separate session. The model can read only the supplied excerpt or task description, with no browsing or additional file access. Its questions and answers will stay out of the later experimental agents’ histories."}],"$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c"]]}],"$L1d","$L1e","$L1f"]}]]}]
14:["$","div",null,{"className":"route-footer","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"The first trial continues by testing use, then interaction."}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/interpretation-layer-poc/phases/","children":["See the three phases ",["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$f:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right","size":18}]]}]]}]
15:["$","footer",null,{"className":"site-footer","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"AI Engineering Playbook · Interpretation layer validation"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Research in progress · Updated as the study develops"}]]}]
