18:["$","$L16",null,{"children":["$","$L17",null,{"id":"guidance-assessment","title":"How will we know that the assessment is reliable?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Build examples containing supported rules, plausible mistakes, legitimate alternatives and statements the evidence cannot settle. Explain the expected assessment from the sources and behaviour, rather than taking another model’s agreement as proof."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Test any model used to verify or assess guidance on separate examples before using its scores. Fix the criteria, error limits and required coverage in advance. Examples used to repair the assessment remain development material."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Assess coverage as well as accuracy. An empty guide should not pass simply because it contains no incorrect claims. Conflicts and valid exceptions matter alongside the usual rule."}]]}]}]
19:["$","p",null,{"children":"We will run these checks when choosing repositories and tasks, rather than during every coding attempt. We will revisit them if the model version or selected material changes."}]
1a:["$","p",null,{"children":"The report will keep all outcomes, including unsuccessful attempts. It will say “familiarity detected” or “not detected by these probes”. It will never describe a lack of detected recall as proof that the material was unfamiliar."}]
1b:["$","p",null,{"children":"Evidence of familiarity will inform whether we use a repository and how we interpret its results. It will not automatically exclude the repository. We will record the selection decision and its reason."}]
1c:["$","p",null,{"children":["The test of missing details adapts ",["$","a",null,{"className":"text-link","href":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.09783","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":"research on recovering omitted benchmark details"}],". It still needs a protocol suited to these repositories. Removing project names is an optional diagnostic, not proof that code is unfamiliar."]}]
1d:["$","$L17",null,{"id":"phase-budget","title":"How will we limit the work and cost?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Before model calls, agree a spending ceiling and limits for drafting, verification, revisions and assessment. Use separate development material for any authorised calibration. Fix the scored run settings before opening its results."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Keep failed preparation and exhausted attempts in the report. The matched budgets for coding comparisons apply in Phases 2 and 3. Phase 1 records preparation costs but cannot calculate savings from code changes it has not tested."}]]}]
1e:["$","$L17",null,{"id":"production-scope","title":"How does this differ from production?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Production would ask a responsible owner to approve or revise the proposed rules. No project owner is available for this POC. We can test whether claims are supported by public evidence, but cannot certify an owner’s unrecorded intentions."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Production would also keep guidance current and serve it during work. This phase assesses a fixed version. Later phases test its use; maintenance remains a possible separate study."}]]}]
1f:["$","$L17",null,{"id":"guidance-examples","title":"See illustrative examples of the guidance","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"NetBox is a public application for documenting network infrastructure. The examples below illustrate guidance about its change history and other project rules. They are shortened explanations, not the exact instructions or selected cases for this phase."}],["$","$L20",null,{}]]}]
